<div class="rt-prose rt-helper-copy">
<div align="justify">
This area presents a button that can help you in the process of making your payment through the use of other methods such as JPesa, Paypal among others.<br /><br />

<b class="rt-strong rt-tone-cardinal">HOW TO COMPLETE THE PAYMENT</b><br /><br />
<ul>
<li>Confirm that the details of the invoice, transaction information that is shown is correct.</li>
<li>Once you are sure that the information is correct, proceed to click on the <button class="btn-xs btn-success"><i class="fas fa-paper-plane"></i> Continue to Payment </button> button and follow the guidelines after until you complete the payment.</li>
<li>When the payment has been confirmed and approved on our side, your product/service will be activated.</li>
</ul><br />
<strong>NOTE:</strong> Should you like to return back to the invoices page, you can click on <a class="btn-xs default"><i class="fas fa-list"></i> Invoices </a><br  /><br  />
<div align="center"><b class="rt-strong">MORE INFORMATION</b></div><br />
The information provided on this page includes invoice details, transaction information, continue to payment button among others which are explained in detail below.<br /><br />
<strong>Invoice Details:</strong> This information is specific to the invoice details and includes information such as amount due which is the expected amount to be paid, invoice number that helps to trace the specific invoice, order IP that shows the IP address from which the invoice was generated to mention but a few.<br /><br />
<strong>Transaction Information:</strong> This information is about the transaction that is being made and it includes the order number, transaction ID, payment mode which in this case would be mobile money among others.<br /><br />
<strong>Continue to Payment:</strong> This is where you will find the button to click that will redirect you to the page where you can proceed to complete the payment.<br /><br />
<strong>NOTE</strong>: It is also possible to open and view the respective invoice should you like to do so by clicking on the invoice number which is given in the invoice details and it will be opened in a new tab.<br  /><br  />

{Msgs::Warning('For more information, please email us on <a rel="mailto:[[CE]]">[[CE]]</a> or call us on <b>[[CP]]</b>')}
</div>
</div>
